course: dictionary
lesson: 13920
title: Leakage: when things get out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A leakage is when something escapes through a hole or crack. The thing that escapes can be liquid, gas or light. «The roof has a leakage, so water drips into the bucket.» The water is getting out where it should not, through a crack. That is a leakage.
explain: Leakage can also mean the amount that escapes. «The leakage from the tank was two litres a day.» Here the word means how much got out, not the hole itself. Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about the hole, or about how much escaped?
explain: Leakage can be about secrets too. «The leakage of private plans to the newspaper upset the team.» Secret facts got out to people who should not have them. The clue is that the plans were private: a leakage of information is when private facts get out.
fact: Leakage means liquid, gas or light escaping through a hole or crack.
fact: Leakage can also mean the amount that escapes.
fact: Leakage of information means secret or private facts getting out to people who should not have them.
fact: A gas leakage is dangerous: leave the place and tell an adult.
fact: Leakage is a noun, so you can say a leakage or the leakage.
exercise: «The bucket catches water from a leakage in the roof.» What is a leakage here? | *Liquid escaping through a crack | A bright light in the sky | A loud noise from the attic | A new kind of roof tile
exercise: «There is a gas leakage, so open the windows and tell an adult.» What should you do? | *Leave the place and tell an adult | Stay inside and close the door | Light a match to see better | Keep cooking dinner
exercise: «The leakage of private plans to the newspaper upset the team.» What does leakage of information mean? | A new computer game | *Secret facts getting out to people who should not have them | Facts written down neatly | A quiet room for reading
test: «Water dripped through the leakage in the pipe.» What does leakage mean? | A loud noise | *Liquid escaping through a hole or crack | A tidy pipe | A bright light
test: «The leakage from the tank was two litres a day.» What is leakage in this sentence? | *The amount that escapes | A kind of water | A new tank | The pump that works it
exam: Why is a gas leakage dangerous? | *Gas can harm you, so leave and tell an adult | It makes the room warmer | Gas is a kind of sweet | It is only water
